<http://data.silknow.org/object/62f64735-d600-3d89-8dd1-29fb7de8d9da>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Panel from a coverlet of pale yellow cotton quilted and embroidered with silk motifs in dark red and cream. \n\nThere is a repeating horizontal pattern: from left to right a peacock with a crayfish, eel or other fish in its beak, a horseman wearing doublet, hose, and a broad brimmed hat, a pair of birds in a tree, a horseman, and a peacock. \n\nThe remaining space is closely covered with flowering plants, deer, hares, a pelican, ducks and other birds. The background has a small lozenge diaper in yellow. Below is a row of rosettes between two narrow stripes of cable ornament."@en , "Panel of quilted embroidered cotton in silks, made in Bengal, 17th century"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/03129ba7-3ba8-3b17-a01c-d9bead03be7c> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Panel from a coverlet of pale yellow cotton quilted and embroidered with silk motifs in dark red and cream. \n\nThere is a repeating horizontal pattern: from left to right a peacock with a crayfish, eel or other fish in its beak, a horseman wearing doublet, hose, and a broad brimmed hat, a pair of birds in a tree, a horseman, and a peacock. \n\nThe remaining space is closely covered with flowering plants, deer, hares, a pelican, ducks and other birds. The background has a small lozenge diaper in yellow. Below is a row of rosettes between two narrow stripes of cable ornament."@en , "Panel of quilted embroidered cotton in silks, made in Bengal, 17th century"@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/62f64735-d600-3d89-8dd1-29fb7de8d9da/dimension/4> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/62f64735-d600-3d89-8dd1-29fb7de8d9da/dimension/1> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/62f64735-d600-3d89-8dd1-29fb7de8d9da/dimension/3> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/62f64735-d600-3d89-8dd1-29fb7de8d9da/dimension/2> ;
        dc:identifier                  "T.113A-1922" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs>
